    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">A binary segment is called balanced if it contains the same number of <const>0</const>s and <const>1</const>s.<br>You are given a binary string <var>S</var>. You are allowed to flip at most one character (change <const>0</const> to <const>1</const> or <const>1</const> to <const>0</const>).<br>Determine the maximum length of a balanced contiguous segment that can be obtained.<br>If no such segment exists, output <const>0</const>.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> A string <var>S</var> consisting only of characters <const>0</const> and <const>1</const>.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> An integer representing the maximum length of a balanced segment after at most one flip.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">1 &le; length of <var>S</var> &le; 10</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">0101</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">4</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
